cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Rig Conductor: from Motif recording to analysed results on a USB disk"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zerotonin/RigConductor"
url: "https://zerotonin.github.io/RigConductor/"
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - aggression
  - animal-behaviour
  - pose-estimation
  - SLEAP
  - loopbio Motif
  - laboratory-automation
  - SLURM
  - Python
authors:
  - given-names: "Bart R.H."
    family-names: Geurten
    email: bart.geurten@otago.ac.nz
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1816-3241"
    affiliation: "Department of Zoology, University of Otago, Dunedin, New Zealand"
abstract: >-
  Rig Conductor is one wizard from "press record" to results on a USB disk
  for a loopbio Motif rig. It records through the Motif REST API, cuts the
  video into one clip per arena, tracks the animals with SLEAP on an HPC
  cluster (SLURM), scores the behaviour and exports the results. A second
  wizard grows a versioned set of hand-labelled frames, trains new pose
  models on the cluster and promotes a model only when it is not worse on
  any validation recording and better on at least one.
